  "query_preview": "..\n(Friday through next Wednesday)\nIssued at 200 PM CDT Wed Sep 16 2026\n\nStrong high pressure in the mid and upper levels will build into\nthe region on Friday and remain in place through the upcoming\nweekend. Although this area of high pressure is expected to weaken\nduring the weekend, we still expect to see well above normal\ntemperatures along with dry weather for most of the region. The\nexception will be near the coastal plains on Saturday as the\nseabreeze may aid in some afternoon showers or storms. In\naddition, the edge of monsoonal moisture may bring a stray shower\nor storm to far northwestern Val Verde County on Sunday. \n\nFor early next week high pressure remains in place, but does\ncontinue to slowly weaken, while a fairly persistent area of broad\nlow pressure remains over the northern Gulf. Developing southwest\nflow aloft and marginal moisture levels may yield some low rain\nchances early next week. However, rainfall amounts would likely\nremain very low. In addition, above normal warmth will persist\nwell into early next week.",
